      },
      {
        "text": "It is uncommon for congressional hearings to effectively elicit answers through well-framed questions.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The purpose of using such a tool is to hold people accountable.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "When we say 'whiteboard someone,' we mean thoroughly presenting the case for accountability.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The method involves framing questions in a way that elicits actual answers.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Effective accountability requires clear, structured presentation of evidence and arguments.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "A whiteboard or similar visual aid enhances clarity and rigor in holding individuals accountable.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Congressional hearings frequently fail to produce meaningful responses due to poor questioning techniques.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Well-formulated questions lead to truthful or substantive answers.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "There exists a standard or expectation for rigorous accountability in institutional settings like Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Rare and congressional hearings, how did you come to realize that a whiteboard could be an effective tool, an effective prop of",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_15",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [],
    "assumptions": [],
    "turn_type_label": "Disrupted",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Before running for Congress, I was a professor. And before that, I taught eighth grade. And so often when a student wasn't following along, when the class was getting a little lost, you would use the whiteboard to lay out the facts, to make the sort of issue at hand clear. And you do that in part because often as a teacher, you would ask a great question only to have the students say, I'm sorry, can you repeat the question? And these corporate witnesses in Congress are coached by incredibly expensive and very talented lobbyists and lawyers. And they're coached to stall, to delay, to ask things like repeating the question, and it makes it hard to get real answers. And so part of the goal of the white board is to help the witness stay on track so they can't worm away, but also to help the American people understand what I'm asking. So while I'm asking about why it's hard for employees to make ends meet on the salary that you pay them, I'm asking a CEO that question. or I'm asking a government official why they won't make COVID testing free given the costs. And so I think a lot of us are very busy in our days. We maybe have a few minutes here there to catch up on what's happening in Washington and whether our representatives are fighting for us. So the white board's a tool to make it easier for people to see what I'm doing in Congress and what questions I'm asking on their behalf.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Before running for Congress, I was a professor.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Before being a professor, I taught eighth grade.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "When students were struggling in class, I used a whiteboard to present facts and clarify issues.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Students sometimes asked teachers to repeat questions due to confusion.",
