  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "We're talking with Orange County Congressmember Katie Porter, and you are listeners are invited to join the conversation. What would you like to ask Congressmember Porter about her priorities in the house, about what she would want to accomplish as California Senator? You can email forum at kqed.org. Find us on Twitter, Facebook or Instagram at kqedforum, or you can give us a call at 867-33-6786-866-73-6786. Well, I do want to ask you, Representative Porter, just about some of your thoughts on recent headlines, one of course being that the Supreme Court agreed to let the abortion drug mythopristone remain on the market temporarily by agreeing to stay a decision by the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals that basically upheld in part. a ban of mythopristone in the U.S. The impacts of the ban would be enormous, as I'm sure you know, and you ran as a self-described pro-choice Democrat. Many experts predict that this decision about whether or not to allow mythopristone will ultimately fall to the Supreme Court, which of course overruled Roe v. Wade. So I'm wondering what you think Congress should do about it. What is Congress's role in this?",
