  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "One of the most important things we have to emphasize here is that this attack on Mepopristone is also an attack on science-based policy. The job of the FDA is not to decide whether a patient should or should not choose to use a drug. Think about the cancer patient who may or may not choose another round of chemo. That's a choice that's up to them. The goal of the FDA is simply to decide whether, based on the science, the drug is safe. And that's exactly what the FDA did in approving methopristor. And so what we see here in this decision is an effort to throw aside safety, to throw aside science, to attack those principles, and to substitute them with an effort to control women's bodies?",
