  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Part of the reason that I'm running for the Senate is I think California needs a political leader who knows how to win tough races. We need people at the top of the ticket in this race in 2024, but also for years to come who knows who know what it takes to talk across party lines, to win over the Republicans that we can, to bring independence into voting because they share our values even if they're sometimes skeptical about whether or not Democrats fight for them. So I think I'm the candidate in this race who knows how to win tough races, and that's something that as Senator, I can help not just help us keep winning in Orange County, but also to win those races in the Central Valley where we've struggled, to win back some of the seats that we have lost. There is no path to the Democrats having a durable majority in the House of Representatives that does not involve us performing better in California than we have. And so I think a big part of what I can contribute as a Senator is I have a track record of knowing how to pull in and engage every single voter and to outperform other Democrats. We saw that in my own race, actually, this fall in 2022. I was the highest performing Democrat on the ticket. I outperformed, you know, all of our statewide officials and all of our local officials. And that is the kind of capacity. to cross-party lines, to win people over without ever compromising California's values that I think we need our political leaders to have. I am very committed to making sure that the area that I currently represent in Orange County continues to be represented by a Democrat who shares our values. I have already endorsed State Senator Dave Minn in the race. And I will do everything I can to make sure that Dave wins. I live in Orange County. My kids are growing up in Irvine. I absolutely am going to fight hard to make sure that we continue to have that representative. Dave represents about 80% of the district already. He's very, very well situated to be reelected to Congress because these people have always already chosen him to be their state senator. So you can count on me to bring the very fight and work and collaboration with wonderful folks who helped and postcarded and knocked doors like Nadine. I want to say thank you to you. We're going to keep that work up. And as Senator, I'm going to be able to help us take the lessons of Orange County and export them throughout California and frankly into every part and pocket of this country.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
