        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Mistreating staff undermines effective job performance.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Public criticism from former employees carries credibility and weight.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Media reports represent a legitimate source of evidence about conduct.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker expects accountability when allegations of misconduct arise.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience values consistency between leadership claims and treatment of subordinates.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Correction / Challenge"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "My staff is top-notch and I am extremely grateful to them. For every whiteboard moment that people see for every successful media appearance or speech that I give, that is a team effort. And one of the things I do in the book very intentionally is devote an entire chapter to talking about how the staff and I work together. And I tell that story from multiple points of view, really giving my staffers their own voices in the story. So I consulted with them and wrote the chapter from a perspective of them sharing what it is like to do the high stakes, high pressure, incredibly important work of Congress. But my staff are incredible exceptional public services. Public servants, we run one of the best most efficient constituent affairs operations, one of the strongest policy shops in the entire Congress, and we pride ourselves on the ability to get the job done for the American people. I have high expectations for myself, and I have similarly high expectations for others who are in public life. whether that's my colleagues, corporate executives who come to testify, or my staff. So when we fall short as a team, I think we have to be honest and direct. We have to talk exactly about what went wrong and how to fix it. So my view is that the stakes are high in this country for democracy, particularly in this moment, and we all want to be delivering our absolute best work.",
