    "turn_text": "For sure. I tuned in a little late and I was just shocked at the difference in questioning a female congressperson from a male congressperson. And it felt like we were back in the 50s when women were asked questions that men are never asked about how they are fathering, how they are taking care of their children, how when they are away, what's happening to the kids. And I just found that so startling.",
