  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 79,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, in my first congressional race in 2018, the most common question that I was asked. I was at a five-way Democratic primary. I had a really tough race against a very entrenched Republican who had cruised to a 17-point victory two years before. The most common question I was asked was what will happen to your kids if you win?",
