    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 83,
    "turn_text": "you're on. Oh, hi. Hi. Yeah. You know, my question kind of builds up on two previous questions. One on Diane Feinstein and, you know, her reluctance to retire at an earlier time. you know, the thought that you're graduating to a safer seat. So I think there's a lot of problems in the sense that, you know, once you're in a safe seat, you don't necessarily push the envelope for progressive values and you just kind of stay maybe longer than what should be. So what are the guiding principles that you'll employ to decide on, you know, when to continue on and when to retire?",
