    "turn_text": "Democrats need to be much more comfortable talking about the economy and about economic issues. And we are the party that delivers lower unemployment, better job growth, fairer taxes. And so we need to be really, really comfortable talking about this. I think the other thing that Democrats need to do is not be afraid to kind of reveal to people that sometimes the problem is us. And I'll give you an example. Last Congress, I fought really hard to try to pass a ban on congressional stock training on Congress",
