  {
    "episode_id": 92669,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92669.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "This Senate race is an incredible opportunity for California to have a conversation about what we want from our next senator. What kinds of experiences do we want them to have? What kinds of fights do we want them to take on? What kinds of political skills do we want them to have? And I think I have some very unique things to offer in terms of my ability to win tough races, in terms of my refusal of corporate PAC donations. And I think in terms of the way I think about oversight as a really important tool to improve people's lives, to make government work better. Both Barbara Lee and Adam Schiff are my colleagues in the California House of Representatives. They're part of the California delegation. And I admire different things about both of their work. If I am very committed to doing this race in a way that boost turnout in California that helps engage more voters and that draws people into a meaningful debate about what California needs from its next senator. We've had a lot of appointments from our governor in recent political history. He appointed Senator Padilla. He appointed the Attorney General, Rob Bonta. He appointed the Secretary of State Shirley Weber. So I think this is a great opportunity for Californians to make their own decision about who they want to represent them. And this is going to be a fun and spirited campaign. It's going to do a lot if we do it right to really fire people up for this 2024 election.",
